---
layout: default-layout
title: Liquify
date: "2026-05-28"
tags: [blog, tutorial]
pageScripts:
  head:
    '/scripts/sync.js'
---

{% assign manager = "npm, pnpm, yarn" %}
{% assign manager_arr = manager | split: ", " %}

<main class="huge">
  <header>
    <h1 class="main-heading large">
      Liquify your
      <span class="huge">life</span>
    </h1>
  </header>

  <article>
    {% comment %} will add TOC later {% endcomment %}
    {% comment %} <h2>Table of contents</h2> {% endcomment %}

    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <p>Firstly create a directory and enter it with the following commands:</p>
    <code>mkdir my-static-site</code>
    <code>cd my-static-site</code>

    <section data-swapping>
      {% for pkg in manager_arr %}
        {% if forloop.first %}
          <details name="pkg_init" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}" open>
        {% else %}
          <details name="pkg_init" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}">
        {% endif %}
          <summary>{{ pkg }}</summary>
          <div>
            <code>{{ pkg }} init{% if pkg != "pnpm" %} -y{% endif %}</code>
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>

    <p>Then open up your terminal and get the following packages ready:</p>

    <section data-swapping>
      {% for pkg in manager_arr %}
        {% if forloop.first %}
          <details name="pkg_install" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}" open>
        {% else %}
          <details name="pkg_install" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}">
        {% endif %}
          <summary>{{ pkg }}</summary>
          <div>
            <code>
              <span data-swappable>{{ pkg }}</span> 
              {% if pkg == "npm" %}install{% else %}add{% endif %} liquidjs
            </code>
            <code>
              <span data-swappable>{{ pkg }}</span> 
              {% if pkg == "npm" %}install{% else %}add{% endif %} -D @11ty/eleventy
            </code>
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>

    <h2>Configuring Eleventy (v3+)</h2>
    <p>Modern Eleventy relies on ES Modules (ESM) by default. Create an explicit configuration file named <code>eleventy.config.js</code> in your project root and add the modern <code>export default</code> structure:</p>
    
<pre><code>export default function (eleventyConfig) {
  return {
    dir: {
      input: "src",
      output: "_site"
    }
  };
};</code></pre>
    <p>This explicitly tells Eleventy to process everything inside your <code>src</code> directory and compile the optimized, production-ready static assets directly into <code>_site</code>.</p>

    <h2>Your First Template</h2>
    <p>Create your source folder structure and your primary template file:</p>
    <code>mkdir src</code>
    <code>touch src/index.liquid</code>

    <p>Open up <code>src/index.liquid</code> and add a front matter block along with a dynamic Liquid array loop to test parsing capabilities:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;---
title: Welcome to Liquify
---&gt;
&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;&#123;&#123; title &#125;&#125;&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;&#123;&#123; title &#125;&#125;&lt;/h1&gt;
  
  &#123;% assign array = "HTML, CSS, Liquid" | split: ", " %&#125;
  &lt;ul&gt;
    &#123;% for item in array %&#125;
      &lt;li&gt;Rendering: &#123;&#123; item &#125;&#125;&lt;/li&gt;
    &#123;% endfor %&#125;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Fire Up the Build Server</h2>
    <p>To keep development moving quickly, add a start script execution path directly into your <code>package.json</code> file:</p>
<pre><code>"scripts": {
  "start": "eleventy --serve"
}</code></pre>

    <p>Now, run the script from your terminal using your active workflow package manager to boot up the hot-reloading development server:</p>

    <section data-swapping>
      {% for pkg in manager_arr %}
        {% if forloop.first %}
          <details name="pkg_run" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}" open>
        {% else %}
          <details name="pkg_run" class="pkg-tab" data-manager="{{ pkg }}">
        {% endif %}
          <summary>{{ pkg }}</summary>
          <div>
            <code>{% if pkg == "npm" %}npm run start{% else %}{{ pkg }} start{% endif %}</code>
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>

    <p>The Eleventy compiler will now build your site and launch a hot-reloading dashboard locally at <code>http://localhost:8080</code>. Open it up and start hacking!</p>

  </article>
</main>